meta {
  name: register (rest-auth path)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/registration/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Same payload as student > registration > register.
    "email": "nueva.estudiante@example.com",
    "password1": "caminante2026",
    "password2": "caminante2026",
    "first_name": "Nueva",
    "last_name": "Estudiante"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Use `POST /student/registration/` instead** -- this is the same view under
  its old path, kept so existing clients do not break.

  It used to be dj-rest-auth's own `RegisterView`, whose default serializer
  created a `User` with no `is_student` flag and no `Student` profile. Such an
  account could authenticate but every portal endpoint rejected it with
  "Student profile is missing". The path now points at the real registration
  view, so that account can no longer be created.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "email_verification_required": true,
    "email": "nueva.estudiante@example.com",
    "message": "Almost there. Check your inbox and click the link to activate your account."
  }
}
